## not_text
discord: Choose a text channel in this server.
plain:   Choose a text channel in this server.
model:   [Fixed("Choose a text channel in this server.")]

## everyone_can_view
discord: Everyone can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, turn off View Channel for the @everyone role.
plain:   Everyone can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, turn off View Channel for the @everyone role.
model:   [Fixed("Everyone can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, turn off View Channel for the @everyone role.")]

## role_can_view
discord: <@&666> can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, remove its View Channel access or choose another channel.
plain:   @Helpers can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, remove its View Channel access or choose another channel.
model:   [Role(RoleRef { id: RoleId(666), name: Some("Helpers") }), Fixed(" can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, remove its View Channel access or choose another channel.")]

## member_can_view
discord: <@222> can view this channel. Remove their access in Edit Channel → Permissions or choose another channel.
plain:   Sam can view this channel. Remove their access in Edit Channel → Permissions or choose another channel.
model:   [Person(Person { id: AccountId(222), name: Some("Sam") }), Fixed(" can view this channel. Remove their access in Edit Channel → Permissions or choose another channel.")]

## quack_missing
discord: In <#444> → Edit Channel → Permissions, allow View Channel, Send Messages, and Attach Files for Quack. Then choose the channel again.
plain:   In #staff → Edit Channel → Permissions, allow View Channel, Send Messages, and Attach Files for Quack. Then choose the channel again.
model:   [Fixed("In "), Channel(ChannelRef { id: ChannelId(444), name: Some("staff") }), Fixed(" → Edit Channel → Permissions, allow View Channel, Send Messages, and Attach Files for Quack. Then choose the channel again.")]

## inaccessible
discord: Quack can't check this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, allow View Channel for Quack, then choose the channel again.
plain:   Quack can't check this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, allow View Channel for Quack, then choose the channel again.
model:   [Fixed("Quack can't check this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, allow View Channel for Quack, then choose the channel again.")]

## missing
discord: This channel no longer exists. Choose another channel.
plain:   This channel no longer exists. Choose another channel.
model:   [Fixed("This channel no longer exists. Choose another channel.")]

## role and member without names
discord: <@&666> can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, remove its View Channel access or choose another channel.
plain:   An unnamed role (ID 666) can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, remove its View Channel access or choose another channel.
model:   [Role(RoleRef { id: RoleId(666), name: None }), Fixed(" can view this channel. In Edit Channel → Permissions, remove its View Channel access or choose another channel.")]
